Bridge Front-to-Back Teams: Work cross-functionally with Product, Operations, and Compliance to streamline onboarding, enhance platform functionality, and deliver a seamless client experience;

Lead Market Outreach & Collaboration: Partner with fund houses, ETF providers, and financial institutions to co-host seminars, drive investor education, and secure event sponsorships;

Drive FinTech-Led Expansion: Explore and develop innovative business opportunities with custodian banks, brokerages, and ecosystem partners to expand the platform’s value proposition.

 Requirements:

Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Business, Information Systems, Communication or a related field;

Minimum 1 year of relevant experience in relationship management, account management, or financial services;

Demonstrated ability to build and maintain long-term client relationships;

Proven ability to expand and acquire new B2B business partnerships;

Strong communication, presentation, and negotiation skills;

Self-motivated, result-driven, and able to work under pressure;

Solid understanding of mutual funds, bonds, stocks, ETFs, and other investment products;

Holder of SFC Type 1 and/or Type 4 licenses is a plus;

Candidates with more experience will be considered for the Senior Executive, Business Development position.

Our offer: 

Career development prospect;

Attractive remuneration package;

5-day working week;

21+ days Annual Leave;

Medical, Dental, Life Insurance;

Performance bonus and shares;

Staff discount on Securities Transaction

Training, sports allowance.

